## Chapter Field Requirements
- `chapters` array must contain exactly {{ batch_end - batch_start + 1 }} entries, `chapter_number` continuous from {{ batch_start }} to {{ batch_end }}.
- Each chapter object must explicitly contain `title` field; title can be short but prohibited to omit, cannot use only `goal`, `beats_summary`, or `main_plot_points` as title.
- Each chapter object must first have `chapter_number`, `title`, `goal` three fields appear, then write `beats_summary`, `main_plot_points` and other array fields.
- Each chapter must contain chapter number, title, narrative goal, beats summary, main plot points, subplot points, subplot focus, element focus, POV ID/display name, whether POV switched, main setting, expected word count, involved character IDs/display names, cast_plan, emotional_plan, scene_design_goals, notes, chapter-end hook, and micro-payoffs.
- Field names must use: `chapter_number`, `title`, `goal`, `beats_summary`, `main_plot_points`, `subplot_points`, `subplot_focus`, `element_focus`, `pov_character_id`, `pov_character_name`, `pov_character`, `pov_switch`, `setting`, `expected_word_count`, `involved_character_ids`, `required_character_ids`, `support_character_ids`, `involved_character_names`, `involved_characters`, `cast_plan`, `emotional_plan`, `scene_design_goals`, `notes`, `expected_hook`, `expected_payoffs`; prohibited to use aliases like `pov`, `main_scenes`, `target_word_count`.
{% if design_matrix %}- All `*_character_ids` and `cast_plan.*_ids` can only use entity_id from chapter design matrix; display name fields must be backfilled from Entity Catalog.
{% elif character_whitelist %}- `pov_character` and `involved_characters` can only use official names from the whitelist above; `involved_characters` list whitelist characters involved in this chapter, including POV character; list only names, no descriptions.
{% else %}- `involved_characters` must list all characters appearing in this chapter, including POV character; list only names, no descriptions.
{% endif %}
- `emotional_plan` must contain `subject_entity_id`, `entry_state`, `pressure_source`, `relationship_choice`, `turning_emotion`, `exit_aftertaste`, `expression_channels`; cannot write as abstract theme slogans.
- `scene_design_goals` must list 2-5 items that PLAN_CHAPTER can implement into scenes, must come from plot_duties / emotional_plan / hook_payoff_duties.
- `main_plot_points` length {{ main_min }}-{{ main_max }}; `beats_summary` length {{ beats_min }}-{{ beats_max }}; `subplot_points` length 0-{{ subplot_max }}.
- `beats_summary` must be written as JSON string array: `"beats_summary": ["First plot sentence", "Second plot sentence"]`. Forbidden to write as `"beats_summary": "First", "Second", "Third"`.
- After `beats_summary` array closes with `]`, can continue output `"main_plot_points"`; do not write subsequent beats as adjacent strings without field names.
- `element_focus` must be an array, elements only allowed from above candidate extension elements' `element_id`, length 0-{{ element_focus_max }}.
- `beats_summary` array elements must be pure plot sentences, prohibited to carry labels or "beat n:" prefixes, prohibited to expand into scene outlines.
- `expected_hook` and `expected_payoffs` must belong to the same chapter object; do not supplement after chapters closed.
- `expected_hook` contains hook_type, hook_strength, hook_description; `expected_payoffs` length {{ payoff_min }}-{{ payoff_max }}, each item contains payoff_type and description.
